Chapter: RocMatchNestedTags
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_match_tests.zig, "match-dt:
 tag payloads destructure through nested tags":

     describe : Try(Try(I64, Str), I64) -> I64
     describe = |v| match v { Ok(Ok(n)) => n, Ok(Err(_)) => -1, Err(code) => code * 10 }
     main = (describe(Ok(Ok(7))), describe(Ok(Err("x"))), describe(Err(4)))     (7, -1, 40)

 Roc's `Try` is spelled `Res` here, a two-parameter sum nested in itself at
 two different instantiations. The tuple is three lines.

Section: Types

  Res (a) (e) =
   | Ok (a)
   | Err (e)

Section: Functions

  describe : Res (Res Integer Text) Integer -> Integer
  describe (v) =
   when v
    is Ok (Ok (n)) -> n
    is Ok (Err (ignored)) -> 0 - 1
    is Err (code) -> code * 10

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (show (describe (Ok (Ok 7))))
   print-line-uni (show (describe (Ok (Err "x"))))
   print-line-uni (show (describe (Err 4)))
  end
